title Fold V -- settle_the_plan, the fossil record, and the fold that cost nothing
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, send the increment.
think Standfast first. Swept crux/REDS.md and both archive ranges for rows booked without a closure. Thirteen numbers came back on a naive grep; reading each showed every one either closed in place, closed inside its own row body, or declared closed by the archive file's own header for rows 88-95. Nothing open and agent-closable, so the line is clear for constructive work.
think Council rota, lap index 584 kyri logs mod 27 -> item 18, context/TWO_ROOMS.md. Deep-read. Its law rhymes with this arc exactly: a claim earns the checkable room only when a witness binds it. The fold queue is a checkable-room number because a scan prints it; the reading of an absentee is checkable too, because the hash decides it rather than the eye.
think Running thread from the top three logs: the Caravan fold arc, folds S, T and U, each recommending the next crux off the printed queue. Two consecutive logs named settle_the_plan as the better crux over the leading provision_notes, whose ninety-one lines stay the body most likely to reach a rung's own wire. Ran the carry meter to confirm rather than trust: provision_notes 2093 across 24, settle_the_plan 1645 across 36.
think Hashed the family before folding it, as folds R through U taught. Thirty-nine files hold a body by that name where the queue names thirty-six -- three standing apart, and the three are not one kind.
think recant.rye differs by exactly two lines: it reaches report_out.recanted and report_out.spared_disproved directly where every rung above reaches them through recanting_of. Fold R's second kind. The accessor it wants was already born -- fold M widened recanting_of in this very file five folds ago -- so two words brought it home and the hash went byte-identical against the canonical.
think bear.rye at twenty-eight lines and appraise.rye at thirty-five are fold R's first kind: dated by shapes born after them. bear.rye predates both the appraisal check and the recantation checks; appraise.rye carries the appraisal and predates the recantation. The three depths read as a staircase.
think The new reading of the lap: an absentee can wear both kinds at once. bear.rye and appraise.rye each ALSO reach their own report directly, exactly as recant.rye did -- report_out.bore in one, report_out.weighed in the other. So the second kind's signature is present in both. Yet no accessor can give a body back a check it never had, so where the kinds meet the dating decides, and the elder stays home.
think Checked every symbol's pub status across all thirty-seven before a line moved. Thirteen functions, one constant, three types -- all already public in every rung. Zero widenings. The arc's second free fold after fold P.
think Generated the harness body from the canonical text by qualification rather than retyping it, so no line could drift in transcription. Folded thirty-seven rungs to an eight-line delegate apiece, each already importing ladder_checks.
think Moved the ceiling in the same commit as the code it measures, and repinned the queue's second family, since a meter whose pins lag its subject has stopped guarding. Rewrote the meter's close line, which had claimed this fold lifted the largest family -- it lifted the second, and the prose now says so.
obs The arithmetic closes with no remainder and names what bringing an absentee home costs. Thirty-five copies gave back 1,645 as the queue promised; recant.rye joining first ADDED forty-seven, making thirty-six copies at 1,692; thirty-six eight-line delegates carry 288. The fall is 1692 - 288 - 47 = 1,357, exactly what the meter measured. The accessor's two words paid for themselves thirty-six times over.
obs A fold pays its successors, read from the other side for the second time. Fold P cost zero because fold O had widened exactly its symbols one lap earlier. Fold V costs zero because the whole arc has been widening this body's reach for twenty folds. A fold's price is set by what its predecessors already made public, rather than by how many rungs it lifts out of.
obs Five laps running, the printed queue has been a lead rather than a verdict, and five laps running the difference has been worth reading. This lap the difference was three bodies of two different kinds, and reading them apart is what let one come home for two words while two stayed home whole.
obs Distinct texts held at 7,868 while bodies and copies each climbed by one. The body the harness now owns is a text the ladder already had, which is what a fold should look like in the count.
